  "rulesRoundTitle": "Rounds and the timer",
  "rulesRoundBody": "A match is five rounds. Each round gives you 60 seconds to pick three cards from hand and place them on your lines. Five rounds of three cards fills all 15 slots exactly.",
  "rulesRoundNote": "Once both players have placed all three, the timer drops to five seconds — your last chance to change what you hide. Anything unplaced when time runs out is placed for you.",
  "rulesRevealTitle": "Face-down placement, simultaneous reveal",
  "rulesRevealBody": "Cards are always placed face down. You see which line your opponent commits to in real time, but never what they played — position and order are information in themselves. When the round ends, every card placed that round flips at the same moment, and revealed cards stay revealed.",
  "rulesVeilTitle": "Veils",
  "rulesVeilBody": "You get three veils per match. Spend one to keep a card of yours hidden through the reveal (tap your own card from this round), or to expose a card your opponent kept hidden (tap their face-down card from an earlier round).",
  "rulesVeilNote": "Hiding and peeking come out of the same pocket — hide now, or save it to read your opponent later. Cards from the current round cannot be peeked; they flip on their own.",
  "tutRevealTitle": "Everything flips at once",
  "tutRevealBody": "When the timer ends, every card placed this round flips on both sides at the same moment. Five rounds fill all 15 slots.",
  "tutVeilTitle": "Three veils",
  "tutVeilBody": "You can keep a card hidden through the reveal. Tap your own card from this round to seal it — that costs one coin.",
  "tutPeekTitle": "Or read theirs",
  "tutPeekBody": "The same coin can expose a card your opponent hid. Hide or read, and where you spend the three — that decides the match.",
